### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@accountId = acc-demo

### 1. Submit a first credit (expect HTTP 202; poll the record to see final status)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-demo-001",
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "transactionType": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "INR",
  "sequenceNumber": 1,
  "idempotencyKey": "idem-demo-001"
}

### 2. Replay the exact same request (expect the original transaction; no second balance effect)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-demo-001",
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "transactionType": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "INR",
  "sequenceNumber": 1,
  "idempotencyKey": "idem-demo-001"
}

### 3. Reuse the key with a different payload (expect HTTP 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-demo-002",
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "transactionType": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 200.00,
  "currency": "INR",
  "sequenceNumber": 2,
  "idempotencyKey": "idem-demo-001"
}

### 4. Submit sequence 3 before sequence 2 (expect PENDING_SEQUENCE initially)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-demo-003",
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "transactionType": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 50.00,
  "currency": "INR",
  "sequenceNumber": 3,
  "idempotencyKey": "idem-demo-003"
}

### 5. Fill sequence 2 (then poll tx-demo-002 and tx-demo-003)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-demo-002",
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "transactionType": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 25.00,
  "currency": "INR",
  "sequenceNumber": 2,
  "idempotencyKey": "idem-demo-002"
}

### 6. Simulate two transient failures (expect eventual PROCESSED with attempts 3)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-demo-004",
  "accountId": "acc-retry",
  "transactionType": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 10.00,
  "currency": "INR",
  "sequenceNumber": 1,
  "idempotencyKey": "idem-demo-004",
  "simulatedTransientFailureCount": 2
}

### 7. Exhaust retries (expect eventual FAILED after 3 attempts)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-demo-005",
  "accountId": "acc-retry-failed",
  "transactionType": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 10.00,
  "currency": "INR",
  "sequenceNumber": 1,
  "idempotencyKey": "idem-demo-005",
  "simulatedTransientFailureCount": 3
}

### 8. Invalid amount (expect HTTP 400 with validation details)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": "tx-invalid-001",
  "accountId": "acc-invalid",
  "transactionType": "CREDIT",
  "amount": -1.00,
  "currency": "INR",
  "sequenceNumber": 1,
  "idempotencyKey": "idem-invalid-001"
}

### Inspect a transaction (replace ID as needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions/tx-demo-001

### List transactions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions

### Inspect balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accounts/{{accountId}}/balance

### Inspect processing summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/operations/summary
